Pins that a backtick command substitution is scanned exactly like the $( ) form -- both inside a double-quoted string (as here) and bare at top level. A backtick span must be located with a matching-backtick, quote-aware walk (a backslash-escaped backtick does not close it) and its contents recursively scanned for a hidden write, the same way $( ) is handled; a write redirect hidden inside backticks must still deny, not be silently allowed as opaque text.
